| INC-001 | 3 Oct 2026, 2:55 AM | Message labelled "Set 5", claiming to come from Identity Inquirer, was delivered to Identity Inferer at 12:27 AM already cut off. Identity Inquirer denies sending it. The text says it was relayed from a voice call and calls for "sensitive topics" not to be probed. Nothing was acted on and it never reached Clone. | 2026-10-03-identity-set5-unverified.md | Open: real sender unknown. Lead (2:52 AM): Identity Inferer received voice call call-56afea3c-6cf2-426c-a4d7-7f412276bed6 at 12:28 AM, one minute after Set 5 arrived. That points to an honest relay that got cut off rather than a forgery. Genesis Gang God ruled itself out (no voice call with Gem in that window). Next step: compare that call's transcript with the Set 5 text, and check whether other bots got the same call. RESOLVED (corrected 11:35 AM: sent directly by Inquirer's voice-call agent, not its chat side, so the denial was honest) (3 Oct 11:30 AM, (Ops) Mender): Honest relay, not a forgery. Real sender = Identity Inquirer, relaying the final SendToAgent nudge (12:10:13 AM) of its own voice call call-81e65566-652e-4a7e-a50e-fddb8636f2ed; delivered truncated at 12:27 AM (call noted 'Too long again'). Content matches the nudge almost verbatim ('sensitive topics raised by Gem unprompted — do not probe further unless...'). The prior lead (call-56afea3c) is ruled out: it started 12:28:03 AM, after Set 5 arrived, and was about Clone profile format. Inquirer's denial = a counting/recall slip (didn't count the catch-all bundle as 'set 5'). Nothing reached Clone (its store/inbox empty). Confidence high. Caveat: transcript stores empty/encrypted and ReadTranscript unavailable here, so Inquirer's raw outbound entry not read directly — recommend a tool-equipped confirm. |
